    "title": "Federal shutdown impacts Home Energy Assistance Program funding - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Nick Aresco ,\n2 hours ago\nCHICOPEE, Mass. (WWLP) – Applications for the Home Energy Assistance Program are experiencing a significant impact due to the government shutdown.\nThe Valley Opportunity Council says that they are seeing an impact on staffing capacity due to federal budget implications, despite demand for their services growing.\nThey are telling people to anticipate delays in processing applications and payments due to the federal government shutdown that started on October 1. The Home Energy Assistance Program will have limited funding beginning November 1st for heating emergencies only.\nTypical annual benefits for fuel assistance that are not emergencies will be halted until the federal government reopens.\nLocal News Headlines ‘Healthcare Heroes’ gala honors eight exceptional healthcare professionals Federal shutdown impacts Home Energy Assistance Program funding Massachusetts State Police recruiting for their cadet program Springfield seeks equitable state funding after casino cuts WWLP-22News, an NBC affiliate, began broadcasting in March 1953 to provide local news, network, syndicated, and local programming to western Massachusetts. Download the 22News Plus app on your TV to watch live-streaming newscasts and video on demand.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WWLP.",
